<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>

<PLUGIN 
  name="motd"
  author="Sebastian Oehm"
  version="2026.10.22.1"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/main/plugin/motd.plg"
  support="https://github.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/issues"
  min="6.11.5"
  icon="fa-desktop"
>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[
###2026.10.22.1###
## New
- UPS module: shows status, battery charge, runtime and load of a UPS from Network UPS Tools (`upsc`), for example the NUT plugin (opt-in, add `ups` to `global.display`). `ups.ups` picks the UPS (default `ups@localhost`), `ups.battery_warn` / `ups.battery_crit` set the battery thresholds (default 50 / 20)
- GPU module: shows NVIDIA GPUs from `nvidia-smi` with temperature, utilization and VRAM, plus the processes using the GPU, labeled by Docker container name where possible (opt-in, add `gpu` to `global.display`; needs the Nvidia Driver plugin). `gpu.warn` / `gpu.crit` set the temperature thresholds (default 80 / 90 °C), `gpu.show_processes` turns the process list off
- Like the other modules, both only list rows that need attention while `warnings_only` is on (the default); set `ups.warnings_only: false` or `gpu.warnings_only: false` to always see the full details

## Fixed
- User Drives / System Drives: the MOTD no longer crashes when `zfs list` fails for a ZFS mount; that drive is skipped instead (reported by Masterwishx in the support thread)
- ZFS drives that report 0 bytes used and 0 available now show 0% instead of a garbage percentage


For older releases, see https://github.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/releases
]]>
</CHANGES>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/motd/unraid-motd-2026.10.22.1-amd64-1.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>https://github.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/releases/download/2026.10.22.1/unraid-motd-2026.10.22.1-amd64-1.txz</URL>
<SHA256>b597b62147206d2437e5d12a06cec35e7424ff5e1b2ce35658c5b41a2c229545</SHA256>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/motd/figurine_linux_amd64_v1.3.0.tar.gz">
<URL>https://github.com/arsham/figurine/releases/download/v1.3.0/figurine_linux_amd64_v1.3.0.tar.gz</URL>
<SHA256>e72430de0ca4b4b4548495d803856f5fec223f43c59a97a0bfcc714710d5032a</SHA256>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'install' script.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[

tar xf /boot/config/plugins/motd/figurine_linux_amd64_v1.3.0.tar.gz -C /usr/local/bin/ --strip-components=1 deploy/figurine

# cleanup old versions
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/motd/unraid-motd-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '2026.10.22.1')
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/motd/figurine_linux_amd64_*.tar.gz 2>/dev/null | grep -v 'v1.3.0')

echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " motd has been installed."
echo " Version: 2026.10.22.1"
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'remove' script.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
removepkg unraid-motd

rm -f /usr/local/bin/figurine
rm -f /usr/local/bin/motd

rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/motd
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/motd
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
